# Overlaid Area Chart Without Boundary Lines

```elixir
Mix.install([
  {:plotly_ex, "~> 0.3"},
  {:kino, "~> 0.18"}
])
```

## Section

Setting `line: %{color: "transparent"}` removes the boundary line while keeping the fill.
This produces cleaner overlapping areas.

```elixir
alias Plotly.{Figure, Scatter}

x = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5]

Figure.new()
|> Figure.add_trace(
  Scatter.new(
    x: x,
    y: [0, 2, 3, 5, 3],
    fill: "tozeroy",
    mode: "none",
    name: "Trace 1",
    line: %{color: "transparent"}
  )
)
|> Figure.add_trace(
  Scatter.new(
    x: x,
    y: [3, 5, 1, 7, 3],
    fill: "tozeroy",
    mode: "none",
    name: "Trace 2",
    line: %{color: "transparent"}
  )
)
|> Figure.update_layout(title: "Overlaid Area Chart Without Boundary Lines")
|> Plotly.show()
```
